I have skipped this thread until now, but happened to read Hal's latest, and
presume the topic has to do with using technology to improve traffic safety (so
that we may improve our chances of a graceful deanimation).

Has anyone mentioned the idea of "pass-through" brake lights which turn on when
the brake lights of the car ahead turn on?  One of many possibilities is that
these would supplement standard brake lights.  The pass-through sensor could
not assume that the car in front had pass-through lights, of course; it would
have to look for standard brake lights (lights of the right color, direction
and spacing, which turn on in unison, etc.)

Unfortunately, my perception is that a technology-based safety innovation which
directly or indirectly causes one horrible accident for every 100 it prevents
will probably itself die a horrible death in the civil courts (again, sorry for
any redundancy).

